  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "Extract the common arithmetic core of the classical constructibility obstructions as a single Lean lemma, prove the full characterization of powers of two, and show the identical lemma drives both the degree predicate `DegreePowerOfTwo p` (Wantzel necessity) and the group-order predicate `IsTwoGroup G` (Galois sufficiency).",
    "plain": "Isolates the single arithmetic fact behind every classical compass-and-straightedge impossibility — that a number with an odd prime factor is not a power of two — and shows the same lemma governs both the Wantzel degree side and the Galois 2-group side of constructibility. Fully verified, 0 axioms / 0 sorries.",
